# Theme-shop README and Sage distribution

When prepping **README.md**, **readme.txt**, **SUPPORT.md**, or the marketplace pack: treat this as a **Sage 11 + Acorn + Blade + Vite 8** theme. Product name is **Walkridge**. Install folder and text domain stay **`walkridge`**. GitHub repo is **`wp-walkridge`**.

## Audience split

| Surface | Audience | Content |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **README.md** | Potential buyers, theme stores, GitHub visitors | Marketable pitch, benefits, what’s included, zip install, link to SUPPORT for tech |
| **SUPPORT.md** | Buyers who need help + developers | SEO policy, plugins, editing, **tech stack**, local Sage/dev, packaging, templates, troubleshooting |
| **readme.txt** | WP / ThemeForest parser | Short description, install, FAQ |

Do **not** dump Sage/Vite/Blade/local-dev/packaging tables into README. Do **not** put local-SEO disclaimers or LocalBusiness/NAP schema talk in README — that belongs under SUPPORT → SEO (regular only).

## README.md outline (buyer-facing)

1. Product title + one-line pitch (tours → guides → shop)
2. Table: live concept, catalog, support, author, **`walkridge`** folder, version
3. Fiction-only callout (`555` phones, `@walkridge.test`)
4. Who it’s for
5. What you get (benefits + blocks/pages/Customizer in buyer language)
6. Regular SEO as a benefit only (title / description / social tags; optional Yoast later) — **no local SEO copy**
7. Quick install from marketplace zip + high-level requirements
8. Link to **SUPPORT.md** for technical docs
9. License GPLv2+

## SUPPORT.md outline (tech + help)

1. Where to start (docs map)
2. **SEO (regular only)** — native tags yield to plugins; explicitly **no** local SEO / LocalBusiness pack
3. Plugins, editing (blocks + Identity)
4. Technical stack, theme templates
5. Local development, packaging
6. Before you file an issue / what the theme does not do

## Repository vs production zip

Git is Sage **source**. Market buyers get a **built zip**. Do not tell a ThemeForest buyer to run `composer install` / `npm run build` on the host.

| Surface | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| Git (`main`) | Blade, PHP, `resources/`, lockfiles. **No** `vendor/`, **no** `public/build/` |
| `walkridge.zip` (`bin/build-theme-zip.sh`) | Runtime only: compiled `public/build`, production `vendor/`, `style.css`, `readme.txt`, `screenshot.png` |
| Outer seller pack | Inner theme zip + child + optional Bookings / Field Map + Documentation |

## `style.css` theme header

Keep Theme Name **Walkridge**, Text Domain **`walkridge`**, License **GNU General Public License v2 or later**, Requires PHP **8.3**, Requires at least **6.6**, Tested up to matching `readme.txt`. Author Matt Hummel / https://matthummel.com/. Plain URLs only.

## Do not

- Lead README with Composer/npm or a “Built with” stack table
- Put local SEO / LocalBusiness / NAP schema language in README
- Commit `vendor/` or `public/build/` to git to “help ThemeForest”
- Put `SELLING.md` inside the buyer zip
- Rename the install folder away from `walkridge` in README “for branding”
- Canonical GitHub repo: `matthummel-pa/wp-walkridge`
